---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
---

<BaseLayout title="How It's Made — BOHUC" description="Follow the material, cutting, stitching and finishing process behind every BOHUC leather piece.">
  <header class="making-hero">
    <div class="making-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / MATERIAL</p>
      <h1>Made slowly.<br />Made to last.</h1>
      <p>Every BOHUC piece passes through one pair of hands—from the first inspection of the hide to the final mark.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="making-hero__image">
      <img
        src={withBase("images/making/step-1.jpg")}
        alt="A selection of colorful textured leather hides in the BOHUC workshop"
        width="1600"
        height="1067"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </figure>
  </header>

  <section class="making-intro" aria-labelledby="making-process-title">
    <div class="page-width making-intro__grid" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">SIX CONSIDERED STAGES</p>
      <h2 id="making-process-title">The process is quiet.<br />The details speak.</h2>
      <p>Leather rewards patience. Rather than rush it through a production line, we work in measured stages so the grain, structure, and edges receive the attention they need.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="making-process">
    <div class="page-width">
      <article class="making-stage" data-reveal>
        <figure class="making-stage__image">
          <img src={withBase("images/making/step-2.jpg")} alt="Blue leather components cut and arranged on a gridded cutting mat" width="1600" height="1059" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
        <div class="making-stage__copy">
          <p class="making-stage__number">02 / PREPARE</p>
          <h3>Cut with intention.</h3>
          <p>Each component is positioned with the direction and character of the grain in mind, then cut individually for an accurate fit.</p>
          <small>Pattern placement · Hand cutting · Grain selection</small>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="making-details">
        <article class="making-detail" data-reveal>
          <figure><img src={withBase("images/making/step-3.jpg")} alt="A leather edge being carefully thinned by hand with a skiving knife" width="1600" height="860" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <div>
            <p class="making-stage__number">03 / REFINE</p>
            <h3>Remove only what is needed.</h3>
            <p>Edges are skived to reduce bulk where layers meet. This small adjustment keeps the finished piece slim and comfortable.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="making-detail" data-reveal>
          <figure><img src={withBase("images/making/step-4.jpg")} alt="A leather wallet held in a stitching pony while being sewn by hand" width="1600" height="1059" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <div>
            <p class="making-stage__number">04 / STITCH</p>
            <h3>Two needles, one strong line.</h3>
            <p>Saddle stitching locks every thread through the leather. It takes longer, but creates a seam made for years of use.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <article class="making-stage making-stage--reverse" data-reveal>
        <figure class="making-stage__image">
          <img src={withBase("images/making/step-5.jpg")} alt="The layered edge of a brown leather piece being finished with a hand tool" width="1600" height="871" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
        <div class="making-stage__copy">
          <p class="making-stage__number">05 / FINISH</p>
          <h3>Build a smooth edge.</h3>
          <p>The exposed layers are levelled, shaped, and finished by hand. Repeated passes create an edge that feels as considered as the face of the leather.</p>
          <small>Shape · Smooth · Seal</small>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="making-signature" data-reveal>
        <figure>
          <img src={withBase("images/making/step-6.jpg")} alt="A brass press applying the BOHUC mark to a leather component" width="1600" height="924" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
        <div class="making-signature__copy">
          <div>
            <p class="making-stage__number">06 / SIGN</p>
            <h3>The final mark.</h3>
          </div>
          <p>Only after the construction and finish meet the standard does the piece receive its mark. It is checked once more, then prepared for its new owner.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="making-end" data-reveal>
    <div class="page-width making-end__grid">
      <p class="eyebrow">MADE IN SMALL BATCHES</p>
      <h2>No shortcuts.<br />No production line.</h2>
      <a class="button" href={withBase("collections/")}>Explore the collection</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
